# Normalise line endings so Windows and Linux tooling stop fighting.
#
# Without this file, git had no policy: files were committed with LF, Windows
# rewrote the working copies to CRLF, and `git status` showed thousands of
# phantom changed lines that hid the real ones. One `git add .` would have
# committed a repo-wide line-ending flip.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` = store everything as LF in the repository, regardless of
# what the working copy looks like.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Arabic story sources are text
*.qalam text eol=lf

# Explicitly binary — never touch these
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary
